      "id": "claim_20e283973d364cbda0b05dcb3efce883",
      "statement": "The float readout is a best-effort plain-text, ANSI-free summary of the selected segments written atomically to a file on each render; it reuses the exact same Segment implementations as the colored path (no second code path) by rendering with the ascii style and stripping ANSI, and any I/O failure is silently swallowed so it can never break the status render.",
